WEBVTT

00:17.700 --> 00:19.500
<i>"To all students,</i>

00:20.110 --> 00:27.140
<i>There has been a string of attacks 
on our students and their guardians.</i>

00:28.390 --> 00:35.290
<i>In addition, many have fallen ill as a result 
of an unexplained loss of magic power.</i>

00:36.610 --> 00:45.240
<i>We are in the middle of 
investigating the causes</i>

00:45.240 --> 00:52.440
<i>behind each incident and their 
possible connections to each other.</i>

00:52.830 --> 00:58.440
<i>In the meantime, we have determined 
that the College is in grave danger,</i>

00:58.440 --> 01:04.350
<i>so for the safety of 
students and staff, we will thus</i>

01:04.970 --> 01:09.910
<i>close the premises, both physically and
 by sorcery, until there is a resolution."</i>

01:24.510 --> 01:27.850
Chise's in London right now, isn't she?

01:31.520 --> 01:33.670
Ow!

01:33.670 --> 01:34.890
Hey!

01:34.890 --> 01:36.720
What's this about?!

03:18.160 --> 03:20.090
You're really leaving the school?

03:21.490 --> 03:25.140
If Grandmother says so, I am.

03:25.530 --> 03:26.920
But...

03:27.370 --> 03:31.860
I was never supposed to be 
here at the College, anyway.

03:31.860 --> 03:37.510
The Sergeant family doesn't think 
very highly of the College.

03:37.510 --> 03:39.850
But your grandmother just said

03:39.850 --> 03:44.340
Philomela's been here because 
the Rickenbackers demanded it.

03:44.340 --> 03:47.530
The Rickenbackers are 
Veronica's family, right?

03:50.170 --> 03:51.590
It's all right.

03:52.930 --> 03:55.370
You don't have to tell us
 if you don't want to.

03:55.370 --> 03:58.360
This is obviously weighing on you.

03:58.360 --> 03:59.560
He's right.

04:00.750 --> 04:03.600
She's not going to talk, anyway.

04:03.600 --> 04:07.590
Seriously, why are you so mean to her?

04:08.240 --> 04:11.100
Why are <i>you</i> so nice to her?

04:13.860 --> 04:15.580
I'd rather not tell you, Rian.

04:15.580 --> 04:16.100
Wha—

04:16.640 --> 04:18.790
<i>This doesn't happen often.</i>

04:19.480 --> 04:24.600
The Sergeant family has served the 
Rickenbacker family for a long time.

04:25.490 --> 04:29.240
I've served Miss Veronica 
since we were little, too.

04:29.630 --> 04:32.390
Which is why I came to the College with her.

04:33.250 --> 04:38.630
B-But then, by "serve," you 
mean she's your master, right?

04:38.630 --> 04:42.720
Why are you suddenly leaving when 
your master ordered you to be here?

04:44.360 --> 04:49.200
I don't know why I was told to come along.

04:50.230 --> 04:52.560
It's like Grandmother says.

04:52.560 --> 04:55.220
I can never do anything right, either way.

04:58.500 --> 04:59.900
Lady Philomela.

05:01.540 --> 05:03.530
I've been looking for you.

05:03.530 --> 05:04.690
Alcyone.

05:04.690 --> 05:06.420
She's from earlier.

05:06.420 --> 05:07.800
It's all right.

05:07.800 --> 05:11.030
She's basically my supervisor.

05:11.570 --> 05:17.490
I'm an artificial fairy made to serve the 
Sergeant family and thus Lady Philomela.

05:17.930 --> 05:19.660
An artificial fairy?

05:20.280 --> 05:24.280
A bodyless entity that's made 
to be a sorcerer's servant.

05:24.780 --> 05:28.620
Fairies can be made artificially?

05:28.620 --> 05:31.270
It's supposed to be pretty
 high-level sorcery.

05:31.750 --> 05:33.260
Correct.

05:34.210 --> 05:39.280
The man who created me 
was a gifted sorcerer.

05:41.600 --> 05:45.770
<i>She kind of reminds me of Elias.</i>

05:46.170 --> 05:48.920
But why is she here?

05:48.920 --> 05:52.590
Are you here to drag her back home?

05:52.590 --> 05:54.240
I've been trapped inside.

05:55.150 --> 05:56.500
Trapped?

05:56.780 --> 05:58.170
Inside.

05:58.960 --> 06:02.870
The College was sealed both 
physically as well as by sorcery.

06:03.390 --> 06:08.630
Because I was given form to accomplish 
some mundane tasks, I cannot leave.

06:09.120 --> 06:13.430
Thus, I will be in your care for a while.

06:13.820 --> 06:15.080
Huh?

06:22.510 --> 06:23.410
Morning.

06:24.300 --> 06:27.110
Morning, Mr. Ainsworth!

06:27.990 --> 06:29.580
Can you get up?

06:30.170 --> 06:31.440
Yes, thank you.

06:31.440 --> 06:32.360
I'm quite a bit better.

06:32.830 --> 06:35.190
The College was sealed off.

06:35.190 --> 06:36.290
Sealed off?

06:36.790 --> 06:39.920
Do we know that the attacker's 
on the outside now?

06:40.430 --> 06:43.890
I suppose that's the question 
this all is meant to answer.

06:43.890 --> 06:45.180
I see.

06:46.480 --> 06:47.540
Thanks.

06:49.320 --> 06:51.880
You came here just to check up on me, huh?

06:51.880 --> 06:53.590
I've gotten myself a great friend.

06:54.930 --> 06:55.770
Eh?

06:57.760 --> 07:01.720
I don't know much about friends,

07:01.720 --> 07:05.210
but you can call yourself that just for 
paying someone a visit while they're ill?

07:06.090 --> 07:08.310
Worrying about someone, caring for them,

07:08.310 --> 07:10.760
thinking about them for no 
reason in particular...

07:10.760 --> 07:13.920
I think that's enough to 
call someone a friend.

07:14.570 --> 07:17.480
If you hated me, you'd 
be glad I'm suffering.

07:18.090 --> 07:19.390
I see.

07:19.950 --> 07:23.860
In that case, I may have several 
friends, including you.

07:23.860 --> 07:24.940
About two more.

07:25.420 --> 07:26.990
That's great.

07:27.500 --> 07:28.820
No, three?

07:28.820 --> 07:30.250
Four?

07:30.590 --> 07:33.760
So they weren't just acquaintances.

07:35.270 --> 07:37.740
My new friend here sure is amusing.

07:48.140 --> 07:51.020
We're allowed to leave the room now.

07:52.120 --> 07:52.940
Okay.

07:53.470 --> 07:54.630
That's good.

08:53.550 --> 08:54.580
Morning.

08:54.580 --> 08:55.340
Did you hear?

08:55.340 --> 08:57.750
We're supposed to gather at the garden 
in our tracksuits for the first hour.

08:57.750 --> 08:59.400
The yard for my class.

08:59.400 --> 09:00.720
What's all this about a closure?

09:00.720 --> 09:03.150
Why do we have to deal with this 
first thing in the morning?

09:05.220 --> 09:08.290
We're supposed to gather at 
the training grounds, apparently.

09:10.120 --> 09:12.230
The College is sealed off? Seriously?

09:12.230 --> 09:14.370
When are they letting us out?

09:14.370 --> 09:17.290
D-Definitely by Christmas, I'd bet.

09:17.290 --> 09:19.250
That's two whole months away.

09:19.250 --> 09:21.770
Are we really safe while we're trapped in here?

09:21.770 --> 09:22.960
Who knows.

09:25.510 --> 09:28.370
<i>I didn't sleep well last night.</i>

09:28.370 --> 09:30.580
<i>I've had too much to think about.</i>

09:30.910 --> 09:32.120
Sleep deprived?

09:32.120 --> 09:33.180
No.

09:33.180 --> 09:34.350
I'm all right.

09:34.350 --> 09:35.480
Fine.

09:36.700 --> 09:39.920
<i>Lucy looks weirdly refreshed.</i>

09:39.920 --> 09:42.220
Lucy! You made it back!

09:42.220 --> 09:43.380
That's great!

09:43.380 --> 09:44.310
Yeah.

09:45.060 --> 09:47.760
I'm not even getting a signal on my phone!

09:47.760 --> 09:49.820
My login bonus!

09:50.260 --> 09:53.070
The curriculum's changing because 
of the closure, too, right?

09:53.070 --> 09:54.570
I wonder what we're doing.

09:54.570 --> 09:57.390
Everyone's talking about the closure.

09:57.820 --> 10:00.940
Apparently closures do 
happen every now and then.

10:00.940 --> 10:02.280
Really?

10:02.280 --> 10:04.630
The College has a number of enemies.

10:04.630 --> 10:07.700
It houses a lot of important 
artifacts and documents.

10:10.230 --> 10:14.660
<i>Anyone with magic and sorcery could get out.</i>

10:15.510 --> 10:18.490
<i>Why did they steal the magic book?</i>

10:19.610 --> 10:22.610
<i>What are they trying to do with 
the magic power they've stolen?</i>

10:24.250 --> 10:26.470
A closure. I love it.

10:27.470 --> 10:30.600
I think it's an interesting 
opportunity, personally.

10:31.810 --> 10:33.240
Zaccheroni.

10:33.930 --> 10:35.820
Why are you here?

10:36.330 --> 10:39.100
Finding people to help during the closure.

10:40.850 --> 10:44.920
You should stop with that 
vicious death glare.

10:47.120 --> 10:48.420
Zaccheroni!

10:50.710 --> 10:52.950
Please stop leaving on your own.

10:53.510 --> 10:55.010
It's Ms. Wachmann.

10:55.360 --> 10:59.000
Sorry, what's the first class going to be?

10:59.700 --> 11:02.810
You know how the school's been 
sealed off since yesterday?

11:02.810 --> 11:06.300
At times like these, you get
 more mandatory lessons.

11:06.300 --> 11:07.970
Mandatory lesson?

11:25.030 --> 11:29.750
Zaccheroni, be sure you keep it 
within the scope of the class.

11:29.750 --> 11:32.030
I know, Wachmann.

11:47.980 --> 11:52.820
Destroy my familiars, and you'll pass.

11:55.230 --> 11:57.950
I'm Fabio Zaccheroni.

11:58.350 --> 12:01.120
This is my supervisor, Sigrid Wachmann.

12:01.930 --> 12:05.460
We'll be providing an important 
mandatory lesson today.

12:11.750 --> 12:14.200
First off, I'll be handing these out.

12:14.200 --> 12:16.110
Don't lose them.

12:18.400 --> 12:20.120
<i>A protective rune talisman.</i>

12:21.130 --> 12:23.590
<i>And modeling clay and a rock.</i>

12:24.450 --> 12:27.430
These talismans make you more resilient.

12:28.070 --> 12:30.230
You know how to use them, correct?

12:31.160 --> 12:33.440
<i>Do I just channel magic power into it?</i>

12:38.740 --> 12:43.490
The fact that the College was sealed off 
means there are enemies on the outside.

12:44.040 --> 12:47.800
Which is why we add these lessons.

12:48.290 --> 12:52.900
The idea is that you should be able to at least 
fight back, should it ever come to that.

12:53.880 --> 12:58.780
Picture a weapon or tool
you might find useful into that clay.

12:58.780 --> 13:00.090
A weapon?

13:08.630 --> 13:10.460
What should I make?

13:10.460 --> 13:12.910
I can't settle on a shape.

13:12.910 --> 13:15.630
Picture something clearly and precisely.

13:15.630 --> 13:16.820
It can be anything.

13:16.820 --> 13:19.750
A knife, a stick...

13:19.750 --> 13:20.950
No guns, though.

13:20.950 --> 13:21.940
There's a trick to those.

13:22.380 --> 13:23.400
Sir...

13:24.180 --> 13:27.150
Why are we using weapons to fight back?

13:27.850 --> 13:30.030
Shouldn't we use our sorcery?

13:35.890 --> 13:39.540
Do you really think you're ready for that?

13:40.220 --> 13:45.000
It's a lot easier to kill by 
stabbing or hitting or shooting.

13:45.440 --> 13:48.600
Or <i>crushing</i>, maybe.

13:52.310 --> 13:53.550
Zaccheroni!

13:56.740 --> 13:57.770
Martin!

13:58.140 --> 13:59.040
Are you all right?

13:59.040 --> 14:01.270
The talismans seem to work.

14:02.070 --> 14:03.600
Are you serious?

14:11.220 --> 14:15.120
Well, get set up and into position.

14:15.510 --> 14:20.070
Just so you know, you'd better take this 
seriously, or it'll hurt pretty bad.

14:28.990 --> 14:30.340
<i>We're trapped inside.</i>

14:31.440 --> 14:33.500
<i>Plus... a weapon?</i>

14:33.500 --> 14:35.870
<i>I've never used a weapon before!</i>

14:45.000 --> 14:46.310
<i>My body...</i>

14:48.960 --> 14:50.500
<i>It's moving on its own.</i>

15:03.450 --> 15:05.300
<i>I never learned to do that.</i>

15:10.240 --> 15:13.790
<i>How can I act so decisively?</i>

15:39.750 --> 15:41.060
It broke.

15:42.710 --> 15:45.290
Wow, you two are fast.

15:45.830 --> 15:48.100
I guess I shouldn't be surprised.

15:48.100 --> 15:49.350
You've got experience.

15:50.940 --> 15:53.060
Wanna have some fun?

15:59.480 --> 16:02.540
<i>I'd be dead if I didn't have the talisman.</i>

16:03.770 --> 16:08.370
I'm not a user so much as I am a maker!

16:21.440 --> 16:24.540
I'm so not cut out for fighting.

16:53.780 --> 16:55.120
Are you all right?

16:59.730 --> 17:01.170
Oh, yeah.

17:01.170 --> 17:02.210
I'm fine.

17:02.210 --> 17:03.360
Thanks.

17:04.940 --> 17:07.530
You didn't get all scuffed up or anything.

17:08.430 --> 17:10.340
You're amazing, Philomela.

17:14.740 --> 17:15.940
Philomela!

17:17.000 --> 17:21.080
I have to be able to do this going forward.

17:22.050 --> 17:24.240
Did someone tell you that?

17:26.770 --> 17:29.800
I think you're awesome, though.

17:48.050 --> 17:49.230
<i>Damn it!</i>

17:49.760 --> 17:52.880
<i>I should have learned how to 
use the spear more from Mom.</i>

17:57.620 --> 17:59.980
<i>I just gotta do what I can—</i>

18:03.660 --> 18:05.740
Done...

18:06.400 --> 18:08.600
Jasmine, your nose is bleeding.

18:08.600 --> 18:10.470
That was pretty rough.

18:11.020 --> 18:13.300
I wonder if everyone else is done.

18:17.230 --> 18:18.540
What's that sound?

18:24.030 --> 18:28.130
<i>My body moves, but I can't do much more 
with a staff than swing it around.</i>

18:38.900 --> 18:39.540
Chise!

18:39.830 --> 18:41.670
Swing it to the side with all you've got!

18:58.680 --> 19:01.740
That's enough, both of you.

19:03.250 --> 19:05.320
Good work.

19:05.320 --> 19:07.460
Everyone's passed.

19:07.780 --> 19:11.000
How could you deny me like that, Wachmann?

19:11.350 --> 19:14.690
I told you to keep it within 
the scope of the lesson.

19:14.690 --> 19:18.990
If you're not satisfied, I'll 
tear you a new one later.

19:22.970 --> 19:26.630
That was good enough for your first time.

19:27.400 --> 19:28.760
Who among you were scared?

19:34.090 --> 19:36.600
You two, don't lie.

19:37.050 --> 19:40.190
Looks like quite a few of you 
had a miserable time, too.

19:40.950 --> 19:44.610
You didn't have time to even think 
about using sorcery, did you?

19:45.090 --> 19:47.610
Do you think you're old enough for that?

19:47.960 --> 19:50.250
Do you think you have the capacity?

19:51.470 --> 19:55.960
Whether you use sorcery or a weapon, 
whether you run away or fight back...

19:56.420 --> 19:59.550
It's up to you in the end 
to take care of yourself.

20:00.080 --> 20:02.720
Think about how you plan to survive.

20:02.720 --> 20:03.630
And...

20:05.010 --> 20:07.020
Don't you dare hesitate.

20:08.440 --> 20:12.350
Got it, my little sorcerers-in-training?

20:14.620 --> 20:16.710
The lesson is over.

20:16.710 --> 20:20.110
Let's have a little chat about 
your teaching style.

20:20.110 --> 20:22.080
Seriously, that hurts.

20:22.080 --> 20:24.700
How are you so damn strong?

20:25.280 --> 20:26.540
Philomela?

20:30.260 --> 20:31.590
What's wrong?

20:31.590 --> 20:33.460
She seems to be feeling sick.

20:33.860 --> 20:35.840
Let's go to the nurse's office.

20:35.840 --> 20:36.990
No...

20:36.990 --> 20:37.990
I'm fine.

20:38.410 --> 20:40.590
You don't look fine at all.

20:48.490 --> 20:51.150
I'll take her to the nurse's office.

20:51.150 --> 20:54.230
Could you please let the next teacher know?

20:54.230 --> 20:55.240
Of course.

20:55.240 --> 20:56.310
Be safe.

20:57.090 --> 20:59.170
I've noticed for a while now...

20:59.170 --> 21:01.410
Chise's pretty strong, isn't she?

21:01.410 --> 21:02.170
Yeah.

21:03.340 --> 21:05.440
Take care of Philomela for us.

21:05.720 --> 21:09.240
She's always been a bit sickly.

21:10.140 --> 21:11.050
Okay.

21:16.380 --> 21:18.840
<i>Veronica knows about Philomela's family</i>

21:18.840 --> 21:22.750
<i>and about how she's being forced to
 leave the College, doesn't she?</i>

21:23.760 --> 21:25.490
<i>I wonder what she thinks of it...</i>

21:33.490 --> 21:34.850
You, too, Lucy?

21:34.850 --> 21:37.600
I used up all my energy back there.

21:37.600 --> 21:40.520
I'll collapse if I'm not close to you.

21:40.520 --> 21:41.620
Ah.

21:42.200 --> 21:44.610
Don't take me to the nurse's office.

21:46.920 --> 21:50.270
Don't be crazy. Look at you.

21:50.270 --> 21:53.490
At least take me to my room.

22:03.630 --> 22:06.360
What's this "dangerous gig" about?

22:06.360 --> 22:08.480
I said it's a <i>good</i> gig.

22:10.670 --> 22:12.040
What the hell?!

22:13.110 --> 22:15.200
Pretty good money, isn't it?

22:15.200 --> 22:17.010
Finding lost treasure.

22:17.010 --> 22:21.930
Specifically, a magic book that's being 
used in some really sketchy ways.
